phrase_check skills/claude-review/SKILL.md "the advice sentence as the final check says" "Advice against the item adds its sentence as \`mentat:review\` \"Final check\" says."
phrase_check skills/review/fast-track.md "the advice sentence as the final check says" "Advice against the item adds its sentence as \`mentat:review\` \"Final check\" says."
phrase_check skills/build/SKILL.md "each item's advice sentence kept in the final message" "with any limit on how it was reviewed and its sentence on advice against it, as \`mentat:review\` \"Final check\" says),"
# Round five ends in a named state; only the maintainer allows more rounds.
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "round five's pushed fixes and status line" "any fixes are pushed, and the status line is \`Not reviewed: no review round left\`, with no \"Ready to merge: #N\" on that head; the maintainer decides."
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "round five with no fixes to push" "With no fixes to push, the state is \`Ready\` only if every Ready condition holds, including that the round covered the current spec"
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "a round five that did not finish or cover the spec" "a round five that did not finish or did not cover the spec is \`Not reviewed: <why>\`, and anything else is \`Blocked: <why>\`."
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "extra rounds allowed by the maintainer" 'The maintainer may say in chat how many extra rounds to allow; a Verification line records the allowance, those rounds run as normal, and the limit applies again once they are used.'
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "no extra rounds without the maintainer, except a removal round" 'Claude Code never allows extra rounds on its own, except a removal round ("Removal round").'
# A push that only removes what the maintainer asked removed gets one more round when none is left, on both paths.
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "the removal round applying whenever the limit is reached" 'When no review round is left (the limit reached on either path, five on the Codex path or two Claude rounds on the Claude-only path, plus any extra rounds the maintainer allowed, whether before or after "Ready to merge: #N"), a push'
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "the removal round's measure against the head just before the push" 'a push that, compared with the branch head just before it, adds no line and removes only what the maintainer asked removed, plus lines that only ran or named it, gets one more review round without asking the maintainer for one.'
phrase_check skills/review/SKILL.md "no removal round on doubt, an added line or an accepted waiver" "Any doubt, any added line, or a push whose waived round the maintainer accepted (\`after-ready.md\` \"Waived round\") takes no removal round."
